            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method of predicting a capacity of a public-transport vehicle for passengers to board at a stop and for displaying information representative of this capacity on a stationary display or on a remote computer device, the prediction process comprises: predicting the capacity of the public-transport vehicle for passengers to board at the stop by measuring a filling level of the public-transport vehicle before the stop and applying a capacity-expectation-modifying parameter adapted to weather conditions, and/or traffic-relevant events and/or public holidays into account in the prediction process, displaying the information representative of the predicted capacity of the train for passengers to board at the stop on the stationary display device and/or on a remote computer device; wherein the public-transport vehicle has a passenger space, and measuring the filling level of the public-transport vehicle comprises scanning the passenger space with at least one measuring device sensitive to the presence of passengers.</p>
            </abstract>
